.TH "JSONKIT" "1" "" "jsonkit 0.0.0" ""
.SH "NAME"
jsonkit \- Read and reshape one JSON document.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBjsonkit\fR [options]
\fBjsonkit\fR <command> [options]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
With no subcommand, jsonkit summarizes the document and its top\-level keys.
.SH "DOCUMENT COMMANDS"
.SS "READ"
.TP
\fBget\fR
Read one value at a path.
.TP
\fBkeys\fR
List the keys at a path.
.TP
\fBstats\fR <command>
Report facts about the document\(aqs shape.
.TP
\fBfetch\fR
Read one value at a path.  (deprecated: Use get instead.)
.SS "RESHAPE"
.TP
\fBselect\fR
Keep the named fields of the document.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.TP
\fBhelp\fR
Show help for a command.
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Check the host this application runs on.
.TP
\fBcompletion\fR <command>
Print or install a shell completion script.
.TP
\fBmcp\fR [command]
Serve this application\(aqs tools to an MCP client over stdin and stdout.
.TP
\fBmanpage\fR <command>
Write or install the man pages.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR <\fIpath\fR>
The document to read. Omit it to read piped text.  (file or piped stdin; \- selects stdin, required)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR <\fIformat\fR>
Select the output format, records by default. One of: records, json, jsonl.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version.
.TP
\fB\-M\fR, \fB\-\-manifest\fR
Print this command\(aqs manifest as JSON.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-explain\fR
Explain the selected command and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-[no\-]color\fR
Turn color on or off, overriding NO_COLOR.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR...
Show more detail. Repeat it for more.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Hide info and success messages.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
\fB$ jsonkit \-f doc.json\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fB$ jsonkit get user.name \-f doc.json\fR
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBjsonkit\-get\fR(1), \fBjsonkit\-keys\fR(1), \fBjsonkit\-stats\fR(1), \fBjsonkit\-fetch\fR(1), \fBjsonkit\-select\fR(1), \fBjsonkit\-help\fR(1), \fBjsonkit\-doctor\fR(1), \fBjsonkit\-completion\fR(1), \fBjsonkit\-mcp\fR(1), \fBjsonkit\-manpage\fR(1)
